# Vercel deployment ignores
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project deploys with plain pip from requirements.txt.
#
# The uv-only files (uv.lock + pyproject.toml) were REMOVED from the
# repo on purpose. Vercel's Python runtime auto-detects those files and
# force-runs its own:
#     uv sync --active --no-dev --link-mode hardlink --frozen --no-editable
# which fails in Vercel's build and ignores our pip installCommand.
# With no uv.lock/pyproject.toml present, Vercel falls back to the
# reliable `pip install -r requirements.txt` (the pinned, small deps).
# All runtime dependencies stay listed in requirements.txt.

# Heavy dev / training artifacts not needed by the serverless function.
test_images/
runs/
models/
dataset/
uploads/
outputs/

# Python caches
.venv/
__pypackages__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
